  "prompt_mode": "short_sentence_continuation",
  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nYour entire life, you've been told you're deathly allergic to bees. You've always had people protecting you from them, be it your mother or a hired hand. Today, one slips through and lands on your shoulder. You hear a tiny voice say \"Your Majesty, what are your orders?\"\n\nAre you the Queen of Bees?  This insect of your shoulder certainly seems to think so, but that's preposterous.  You think that you must just be hearing things, so you carefully brush the bee away and try to get away from it.\n\nBut the bee returns, and it asks again \"What are your orders, Your Majesty?\"\n\n\"Well, it can't hurt to try\" you think to yourself, and you say \"First of all, avoid all physical contact with me.\"\n\nThe bee flies a few inches above you and says \"Affirmative.  How may I proceed?\"",
